msgid ""
"[[quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token]]`link:#quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token[quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token]`\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"Verify CSRF token in the CSRF filter. If this property is enabled then the input stream will be read and cached by the CSRF filter to verify the token. If you prefer then you can disable this property and compare CSRF form and cookie parameters in the application code using JAX-RS javax.ws.rs.FormParam which refers to the `form-field-name` form property and javax.ws.rs.CookieParam which refers to the `CsrfReactiveConfig++#++cookieName` cookie. Note that even if the CSRF token verification in the CSRF filter is disabled, the filter will still perform checks to ensure the token is available, has the correct `token-size` in bytes and that the Content-Type HTTP header is either 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' or 'multipart/form-data'.\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_CSRF_REACTIVE_VERIFY_TOKEN+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

msgid "[[quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token]]`link:#quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token[quarkus.csrf-reactive.verify-token]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Verify CSRF token in the CSRF filter. If this property is enabled then the input stream will be read and cached by the CSRF filter to verify the token. If you prefer then you can disable this property and compare CSRF form and cookie parameters in the application code using JAX-RS javax.ws.rs.FormParam which refers to the `form-field-name` form property and javax.ws.rs.CookieParam which refers to the `CsrfReactiveConfig++#++cookieName` cookie. Note that even if the CSRF token verification in the CSRF filter is disabled, the filter will still perform checks to ensure the token is available, has the correct `token-size` in bytes and that the Content-Type HTTP header is either 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' or 'multipart/form-data'."
msgstr ""

msgid "Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_CSRF_REACTIVE_VERIFY_TOKEN+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"[[quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded]]`link:#quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded[quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded]`\n"
"\n"
"[.description]\n"
"--\n"
"Require that only 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' or 'multipart/form-data' body is accepted for the token verification to proceed. Disable this property for the CSRF filter to avoid verifying the token for POST requests with other content types. This property is only effective if `verify-token` property is enabled.\n"
"\n"
"Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_CSRF_REACTIVE_REQUIRE_FORM_URL_ENCODED+++[]\n"
"--"
msgstr ""

msgid "[[quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded]]`link:#quarkus-csrf-reactive_quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded[quarkus.csrf-reactive.require-form-url-encoded]`"
msgstr ""

msgid "Require that only 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' or 'multipart/form-data' body is accepted for the token verification to proceed. Disable this property for the CSRF filter to avoid verifying the token for POST requests with other content types. This property is only effective if `verify-token` property is enabled."
msgstr ""

msgid "Environment variable: env_var_with_copy_button:+++QUARKUS_CSRF_REACTIVE_REQUIRE_FORM_URL_ENCODED+++[]"
msgstr ""

msgid "About the Duration format"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The format for durations uses the standard `java.time.Duration` format.\n"
"You can learn more about it in the link:https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/time/Duration.html#parse-java.lang.CharSequence-[Duration#parse() javadoc]."
msgstr "O formato para durações usa o formato padrão `java.time.Duration` . O senhor pode saber mais sobre isso no link:https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/api/java/time/Duration.html#parse-java.lang.CharSequence-[javadoc Duration#parse()] ."

#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"You can also provide duration values starting with a number.\n"
"In this case, if the value consists only of a number, the converter treats the value as seconds.\n"
"Otherwise, `PT` is implicitly prepended to the value to obtain a standard `java.time.Duration` format."
msgstr "O senhor também pode fornecer valores de duração que comecem com um número. Nesse caso, se o valor consistir apenas em um número, o conversor tratará o valor como segundos. Caso contrário, `PT` é implicitamente anexado ao valor para obter um formato padrão `java.time.Duration` ."

